Well, not to delve to deeply into a religious discussion, there is a 
case to be made that the Commandments, or maybe 'morality' in general, 
is a sort of compressed, codified practicality.  Like the prohibition 
towards pork, for instance, doesn't make much sense today, but only 
because safe processing has become so much more prevalent.  Back then, 
eating pork had a good chance of making a person *really* sick.

Don't kill people?  Even if they piss you off?  Well, that's no fun!  It 
is ruthlessly practical, though.  A person, alive, is a resource you 
might be able to tap later.  Dead.... well, about all you can do is 
check his pockets for loose change.  Oh, and if you want to be 
sentimental, there's that whole "every life has value" thing... ;)

Don't "bear false witness"?  That means telling lies, right?  Some also 
interpret it to prohibit gossiping, too.  The practical side is that 
sticking to the truth and not blabbing about other people makes life 
simpler, because you don't have to track who knows what.

That said, I think I'm gonna have to say that honoring Izchak's memory 
by safeguarding his in-game avatar is something that doesn't belong in 
this list as it stands.

That would make it more of a community binding commandment rather than a 
  guide to the path of success for Nethack.

